{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sports and Leisure", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Stunt Acts", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Describe detailed facts about events or actions in work and social contexts, in written or spoken situations", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Adverbial Clauses: When, Where, How and Why", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " An <span class=\"strong\">adverbial clause </span>is a group of words which have the same function as an adverb. Like all clauses, an adverbial clause has a subject and a verb.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">Adverbial clauses of time</span> are used to express when something happens or how often something happens. You can use a <span class=\"strong\">subordinating conjunction</span> like <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">after</span></span>, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">as</span></span>, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">as long as</span<span class=\"italic\">,<span class=\"strong\"> as soon as</span></span> or<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> until</span></span></span>   to introduce the adverbial clause. <br>Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'm going to register at my local gym as soon as I get paid.<br/> I'll train until I start seeing results.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">Adverbial clauses of place </span>are used to express where something happens. An adverb of place often starts with a preposition like <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> in</span></span>, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">on</span></span> or <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">near</span></span>. <br/> You can use a <span class=\"strong\">subordinating conjunction</span> like <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">anywhere</span></span>, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">everywhere</span></span>, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">where</span></span> or <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">wherever</span></span> to introduce the adverbial clause.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Danielle tries to climb a mountain wherever she travels to.<br/> She is willing to travel anywhere mountains can be found.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\"> Adverbial clauses of manner</span> are used to express how something happens. An adverb of manner often starts with a <span class=\"strong\"> subordinating conjunction</span> like <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> as</span></span>, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\"> like </span></span>or <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\"> the way\u2026</span></span>  to introduce the adverbial clause. <br>Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Bungee jumpers still jump from cliffs the way the original creators of the sport had intended.<br/> They see danger as an unnecessary feeling that gets in the way of enjoying the jump into the void.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\"> Adverbial clauses of cause </span>are used to express how something happens. An adverb of cause often starts with a <span class=\"strong\">subordinating conjunction </span>like <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">as</span></span>, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">because</span></span>, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">given</span></span> or <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">since \u2026 </span></span> to introduce the adverbial clause.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Organizers didn't know how to prevent the accident, given the short time it took for Gina to perform her jump.<br/> Since Gina was a celebrated world-class jumper, the organizers thought everything would go according to plan.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When people choose a movie or television show to watch, they tune in because they want to see their favorite actors or a thrilling story.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Wherever films are being produced, some of the most important people on the set are the stunt people.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It is rarely a gratifying profession, given that the glorified lead actors seem to get all the credit.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Many \"learn the ropes\" by doing the actual job, the way a welder or an artist might.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Report Facts or Talk About Untrue or Possible Events", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">active voice </span>when you want the \u2018doer' of the action to be the subject.<br/> You use the<span class=\"strong\"> passive voice</span> when you want the \u2018receiver' of the action to be the subject.<br/> You can use the <span class=\"strong\">passive voice </span>when you want to report events that happened in the past in a general way.<br/> You use the <span class=\"strong\">passive form of Modal verbs </span>to put the emphasis on the receiver of the action, and to suggest possibility, certainty, injunction or prohibition.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"bullet\">Most of spoken English uses <span class=\"strong\"> active speech</span>. When you use an <span class=\"strong\"> active sentence</span> to report an event, the subject is the focus of the sentence.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Extreme Sports Africa (subject) organized this centenarian's jump (object). </li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"bullet\">A <span class=\"strong\"> passive sentence </span>puts the emphasis on the object of the active sentence. When you use a <span class=\"strong\"> passive sentence</span> to report an event, the object of the active sentence now becomes the subject and focus of the passive sentence.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>This centenarian's jump (subject) <span class=\"strong\">was organized by</span> Extreme Sports Africa (object).</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"bullet\">You can use the<span class=\"strong\"> Simple Past passive</span> form to report events in an impersonal way. The subject is not specific, but general.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li><span class=\"strong\">It was reported that</span> Marion Van Loon became the first person over 100 to parachute out of a plane.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"bullet\">You make the <span class=\"strong\">passive form</span> of a verb by using tenses of the be verb followed by the past participle. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"bullet\">As with other verbs, the<span class=\"strong\"> passive form of modal verbs</span> puts the emphasis on the receiver of the action and not on the doer of the action. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"bullet\"><span class=\"strong\">Passive modal forms </span>are often impersonal and do not require an object.<br/> Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Bungee jumping should be enjoyed in a safe and responsible environment.<br/> <li>Some of the best jumps in the world may be enjoyed from these cliffs.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"bullet\">The structure of <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present passive for modal verbs</span> is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "subject+modal verb+be+past participle of verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"bullet\">You can use <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present modal verbs</span> to convey a general obligation or a permission.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of Simple Past passive for modal verbs is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "subject+modal verb+have been+past participle of verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>Bungee jumping must have been seen as a rite of passage.<br/> <li>Bungee jumping might have been introduced to the western world by Captain James Cook, though no one is really sure about that historical fact.</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use Simple Past modal verbs to convey certainty, possibility, or uncertainty about a past event or situation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They were reported to have worked without the help of nets or safety harnesses.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Eventually, stunt performers were employed by live theater acts, and finally by early cinema.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Audiences must have been alarmed to see these daredevils free falling with no protection whatsoever.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The earliest stunts were performed by circus acrobats.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "distressing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "upsetting or worrying", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How do stunt people prepare for their distressing and unsettling job?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about adventurous jobs.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "exhilarating", "type": "name"}, {"content": "causing a feeling of excitement", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Being a stunt person is an exhilarating and difficult profession.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gratifying", "type": "name"}, {"content": "satisfying or pleasing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is rarely a gratifying profession.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "satisfied ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "contented or pleased", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The stunt people must be satisfied with having participated in the production.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "glorified", "type": "name"}, {"content": "important or honored", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The glorified lead actors seem to get all the credit. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "thrilling", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very exciting or exhilarating", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They tune in because they want to see their favorite actors or a thrilling story.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "unsettling ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "disturbing; makes you feel worried", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How do stunt people prepare for their distressing and unsettling job?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le02ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Research a profession that you know very little about. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make notes on the history of the profession.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make notes on the the training requirements for one who chooses this profession.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your findings to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research an unknown profession.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give background information.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about how something is done.",